{"Several places where the dark-theme lightness ratio looks inconsistent with the light-theme value (e.g. .custom-message-length in mobile goes from 70% to dark-light-choose(primary 30%, secondary 70%), and some other spots swap 20%/80% or 30%/70%) - need to verify these were intentional and visually balanced": 0.42601582407951355, "Mobile custom-message-length color lightness is inverted compared to desktop and the previous implementation - the change switches to 30% for $primary and 70% for $secondary, inverting the contrast hierarchy. Should align mobile rule with desktop one to keep contrast and visual weight consistent.": 0.6893864870071411, "Consider introducing a small Sass helper/mixin for the dark-light-choose(scale-color($primary, ...), scale-color($secondary, ...)) pattern to reduce repetition and make future theme tuning easier": 0.02476639859378338}